body:
The functionality of slashing the bond corresponding to the failed proposals exits to avoid spam on-chain. So proposing to reimburse the bond amount for the failed proposals as long as those proposals are not spam.

**Recently failed proposals:**
- Creation of sign language-based tutorials around the Edgeware for people with disabilities. {Bond: 519750, bond signer: Decent Partners}
- SCU Proposal: November 2022 {Bond: 3109392.2, bond signer: Zovern}


**The proposal which is likely to fail (based on the voting so far):**
- Richard Welsh, Edgeware R&D October / November invoice 4 {Bond: 1406454.05, bond signer: Decent Partners (Jan lent 1M EDG and MoonY lent 500k EDG to Decent Partners)} 


## Clauses:
1. The total of bonds' reimbursements [5035596.25 EDG] is proposed for treasury spending (subject to a public referendum) to a 3/5 multi-sig with Rich, Zovern, Jan, MoonY and Shankar as signers.
2. If in case Referendum #134 passes, the corresponding bond amount of 1406454.05 EDG will be sent back to the treasury. {In this case, the distribution will be 519750 EDG to Decent Partner and  3109392.2 EDG to Zovern.}
3. Distribution of the reimbursements in case of Referendum #134 gets rejected, is as follows:
- Zovern: 3109392.2 EDG
- Decent Partners: 426204.05 EDG {519750 + 1406454.05 - 1000000 - 500000}
- Jan: 1000000 EDG
- MoonY: 500000 EDG



Multi-sig address (3/5): oFmpR8mnR2pZ7zfwnjF4PAPvE5DwGujYTXeuv55U8Fpkwng
Total of bonds' reimbursements: 5035596.25 EDG
